    "within": "Questions 1 to 3 tap-count a tidy row of 1, then 2, then 3 objects. Question 4 types the count of 4 on a five-frame. Question 5 builds a group of 5 from a tray. Question 6 says what comes next. Question 7 picks the missing amount in the count from pictures. Question 8 orders 1 to 3. Question 9 matches numerals to amounts. Question 10 is a short story: Sam needs 5. The object counts climb 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 with no drop-back.",
    "versus": "Easy: tidy rows, tap to count, one step, hints on the first three items. Medium uses scattered groups, mixed pictures and numerals, and count draws inside 2 to 5. Hard mixes in extra objects to ignore, number words, and a full 1 to 5 order, still within 5. Hard does not teach bonds or composition of 5."
